      "name": "Baby Sweet Onion",
      "description": "Fresh sweet onions are characterized by their mild, sweet flavor and relatively low pungency compared to other onion varieties. They are often larger than yellow onions and have a flatter, rounder shape. Their thin, papery skin can be yellow or light brown, and the flesh inside is translucent, juicy, and crisp. These onions are great for raw consumption in salads, sandwiches, and relishes, and also excel when cooked, especially in dishes requiring caramelization or onion rings.",
